    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer planar dielectric stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat), HfO2, SiO2 (Kischkat) (alternating, starting with HfO2, ending with SiO2 (Kischkat) before substrate). All 20 layer thicknesses are independent optimization variables with bounds 200-3000 nm. Wavelength bands: 3000-5000 nm (suppress emissivity) and 8000-13000 nm (maximize emissivity). Polarization: unpolarized or both TE and TM averaged. Incidence angle: 0 degrees (normal). Objective: maximize emissivity contrast between the two bands using gradient thickness optimization with quadratic penalty weight 0.02 and perturbation bound ±0.2%. Material names must resolve to hfo2, SiO2 (Kischkat), and si from the catalog. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates.",
